<!--
    GH-1916 (kuna): "x86-64: a seventh int argument clang stores over a pushed
    pad prints the pad register's upper half"
    https://github.com/Noelo-Lab/kuna/issues/1916

    Source:
      int in7(int,char**,const char*,void*,int*,int,int);
      long il7(int,char**,const char*,void*,int*,int,long);
      int ic7(int,char**,const char*,void*,int*,int,char);
      int pr(const char *, ...);
      int k7(void){return in7(1,0,0,0,0,6,7);}
      int kc(char c){return ic7(1,0,0,0,0,6,c);}
      int kp(void){return pr("%d %d %d %d %d %d\n",1,2,3,4,5,6);}
      long kl(long x){return il7(1,0,0,0,0,6,x*3);}

    clang -O2 for x86_64-linux-gnu, linked at 0x100000 with the format string
    at 0x100400 and the callees left as bare addresses (in7 0x100800, ic7
    0x100810, pr 0x100820, il7 0x100830).  clang aligns the stack for each
    call with `push %rax` and stores the seventh argument over the low four
    bytes of that slot (`movl $7,(%rsp)`; `movl %edi,(%rsp)` in kc).

    Stage model: P4 call recovery, active-input-trial scoring.  The 8-byte
    stack trial pieces the stored value with the upper half of the caller's
    incoming RAX, which the System V model never takes as a parameter, and in
    kc also with bytes 1-3 of rdi above the declared char.  The calls printed
    `CONCAT44(v1,7)`, `CONCAT44(v1,(int)CONCAT71(v2,c))` and
    `(unsigned long)v1 & 0xffffffff00000000 | ...6...` with v1 never set.
    kuna_stackpadarg.rs (always on) narrows the trial to its low bytes below
    that padding.  kl stores a whole computed long, which stays 8 bytes.
-->
